{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 46, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind in Japan**\n\nTokyo’s neon glow greeted me as I stepped off the train—skyscrapers hummed with life while tiny izakayas beckoned below. My first night ended in a ramen shop at 3 AM, slurp-sticks clacking in harmony with the sizzle of pork broth.\n\nKyoto unfurled like a watercolor painting—cherry blossoms dusted the temples of Kiyomizu-dera, their petals scattered on stone paths. At dawn, I joined monks chanting at Todai-ji, the Great Buddha’s wooden face serene under golden light. Tea in a matcha café with a geisha’s grace (okay, just a very polite server) was the cherry on top.\n\nOsaka’s energy was pure chaos. I crammed takoyaki into my mouth on Dotonbori’s street, dodging crowds to scream for a photo with a giant pufferfish. Universal Studios Japan’s Harry Potter ride was worth the wait—magic in motion.\n\nHiroshima’s Peace Memorial Park was quiet. I knelt among the cranes of *Sadako and the Thousand Paper Cranes*, their messages for peace as moving as the city’s resilience.\n\nThe Bullet Train zoomed me home, but Japan lingered—the taste of matcha, the scent of incense, the hum of vending machines offering hot coffee at midnight. A country where tradition dances with the future, one bite, bow, and bullet train at a time.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.06942010670900345}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.35668447613716125}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.04385815188288689}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.0221111997961998}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": -8.666139910928905e-05}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -1.362950325012207}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.42458853125572205}, {"token": "**\n\n", "logprob": -2.831692934036255}, {"token": "Tokyo", "logprob": -1.1522916555404663}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.40679189562797546}, {"token": " neon", "logprob": -0.18847498297691345}, {"token": " glow", "logprob": -0.2